    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Qk3mNMWWpAkGQrx9doyvXp)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent: based on `main`, no dependencies.\n- Touches `sp-org-base` (new command), `sp-keys` (one binding), the keymap design doc and two test files.\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n- Branch name is not number-prefixed (cloud sessions cannot rename it); this should be #543.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Key chosen: `C-; \"`** (leader, then Shift-'), global, two keys instead of `C-c C-,` then `q` and a paste.\n- Why this key:\n  - on the leader root, not under a group, so it is as short as it can be\n  - letters at the root are group names; punctuation is free (only `.` is used)\n  - no CUA keys (`C-z/c/x/v`), no Alfred (Cmd+Space), no Ctrl+Space; GUI-only like the rest of the leader\n- New command `sp-org-insert-quote-from-kill` in `sp-org-base`:\n  - fills the block with `(current-kill 0 t)`, the ring is not rotated or changed\n  - active region: the region is cut and put in the block instead\n  - `C-u` (and no region): empty block; empty kill ring: empty block, no error\n  - starts on its own line (inserts a newline when point is mid-line)\n  - trailing newlines dropped, text properties dropped, lines starting with `*` or `#+` escaped with a comma\n  - point ends after `#+end_quote` (inside the block when it is empty)\n- Binding and autoload in `sp-keys`; docs (bullet lists) in `sp-org-base.org`, `sp-keys.org` and `global-keymap-namespaces.org` (\"Root keys\").\n- Tests (Emacs 29.3): 10 new in `tests/sp-org-base-quote-test.el`, 1 new in `tests/sp-keys-test.el`; all pass.\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh`: only these two docs (other drift is the known Org-version artifact, not committed).\n- `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n- Not run: the GUI.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Copy a paragraph, press `C-; \"` in an Org buffer: a quote block with it appears, point after `#+end_quote`\n- [ ] Press `C-y`-equivalent paste afterwards: the kill ring still starts with the same item\n- [ ] Select some text, `C-; \"`: the region is wrapped in a quote block\n- [ ] `C-u C-; \"`: an empty block, point inside it\n- [ ] With point mid-line: the block starts on a new line\n- [ ] `C-; c o` then `q` (`org-block-wrap`) still works\n- [ ] `C-h k C-; \"` shows `sp-org-insert-quote-from-kill`; which-key at `C-;` lists `\"`\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8raozNvfBNq7hXbpR)_",
